Requirements
-Use Android custom View drawing APIs only. Do not use Compose, PopupWindow, Dialog, MotionLayout, or third-party overlay libraries.
-Target bounds are in this view’s local pixel coordinates. setTargets must reject duplicate target ids with IllegalArgumentException.
-If there is no active target, the active id is unknown, the target bounds are malformed, or the target is fully outside the view, draw nothing.
-Draw a dim overlay over the full view using color #99000000, then cut a transparent spotlight hole for the active target.
-The spotlight uses the visible portion of the target bounds clipped to the view. Expand that clipped target by 8dp before cutting the hole.
-RoundedRect spotlight holes use 12dp corner radius. Circle spotlight holes use radius max(width, height) / 2 after the 8dp expansion.
-setTooltipSize(widthPx, heightPx) requires both values to be positive; otherwise throw IllegalArgumentException.
-The tooltip bubble is a white rounded rectangle with 8dp corner radius. It must be placed using this priority order: bottom, top, end, start.
-A candidate tooltip placement fits only if the whole bubble is inside the view. Bottom/top are horizontally centered on the visible target center. Start/end are vertically centered on the visible target center. The tooltip gap from the expanded spotlight bounds is 8dp.
-In LTR, start means left and end means right. In RTL, start means right and end means left.
-If no candidate fully fits, choose the candidate with the largest area inside the view before clamping; break ties using the same priority order. Then clamp the bubble fully inside the view.
-Draw a white triangular arrow from the bubble edge toward the visible target center. After tooltip clamping, the arrow must still point to the visible target center.
-Switching active targets, changing tooltip size, changing layout direction, or resizing the view must recompute all cutout, tooltip, and arrow geometry from current inputs. No stale geometry may be reused.
-Drawing must be deterministic enough for Robolectric bitmap tests and Roborazzi screenshot tests.







