# Important Tests

1. [Robolectric/Bitmap] transparent cutout over dim overlay  
Place one active target in the center. Verify pixels inside the spotlight hole are transparent and pixels outside it are dimmed with `#99000000`.

2. [Robolectric/Bitmap] only active target is cut out  
Set multiple valid targets and activate one. Verify only the active target has a transparent cutout, then switch active id and verify the old cutout disappears.

3. [Robolectric] duplicate target ids rejected  
Call `setTargets` with two targets using the same id. Verify `IllegalArgumentException`.

4. [Robolectric/Bitmap] centered target chooses bottom tooltip  
Use a centered target with enough room on all sides. Verify the tooltip is below the expanded spotlight bounds because bottom has highest priority.

5. [Robolectric/Bitmap] edge targets choose alternate placements  
Place targets near bottom, top, left, and right edges. Verify placement falls back to top, bottom, end, or start according to the priority order and available space.

6. [Robolectric/Bitmap] RTL start/end placement  
Use a side-placement case where vertical placements do not fit. Verify LTR and RTL choose mirrored start/end positions.

7. [Robolectric/Bitmap] huge tooltip fallback clamps inside view  
Use a tooltip too large to fit in any preferred position. Verify the chosen fallback has the largest pre-clamp visible area, then the final bubble is fully clamped inside the view.

8. [Robolectric/Bitmap] arrow still points after clamping  
Use a corner target and oversized tooltip so clamping occurs. Verify the arrow tip points toward the visible target center, not the unclipped target center or old bubble position.

9. [Robolectric/Bitmap] partially offscreen target  
Use a target partly outside the view. Verify the spotlight is based on the clipped visible target, the cutout stays inside the view, and the arrow points to the visible target center.

10. [Robolectric/Bitmap] circle and rounded-rect spotlight geometry  
Render the same rectangular target once as `Circle` and once as `RoundedRect`. Verify the circle uses the expanded max dimension as radius and the rounded rect uses `12dp` corners.

11. [Robolectric] resize recomputes placement  
Draw with one view size, then resize so the previous tooltip placement no longer fits. Verify the tooltip and arrow are recomputed, not reused.

12. [Robolectric] layout direction change recomputes placement  
Draw a side-placement case in LTR, switch to RTL, redraw, and verify the tooltip mirrors correctly.

13. [Robolectric/Bitmap] deterministic output  
Render the same targets, active id, tooltip size, layout direction, and view size twice. Verify identical bitmap output.

14. [Roborazzi] crowded-corner fallback visual  
Capture a corner target with a large tooltip. Verify dim overlay, clipped spotlight, clamped tooltip, and arrow direction together.

15. [Roborazzi] partially offscreen visual  
Capture a target partly outside the view. Verify the clipped cutout and tooltip placement look stable.






